ge (shrunken to global) ===\\\")\nfor node_shrink in [0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.5]:\n    for node_alpha in [100, 1000, 10000]:\n        mae, std = cv_evaluate(\n            lambda f, t: fit_pernode_ba(f, t, node_alpha=node_alpha, node_shrink=node_shrink),\n            pred_pernode_ba\n        )\n        print(f\\\"  shrink={node_shrink:.1f}, alpha={node_alpha:5d}: MAE={mae:.4f} +/- {std:.4f}\\\")\n\n# Let's also try: per-node intercept only (bias correction) on top of global model\n# This is essentially what we had before but with per-horizon per-node bias\n# Let's compare to the previous best\n\n# Previous best (reference): base+anchor Ridge + node bias + NH bias = 14.52\n# Let me try a version with graph-smoothed per-node coefficients\n\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"=== Per-node base+anchor Ridge (shrunken to global) ===\n  shrink=0.1, alpha=  100: MAE=14.4757 +/- 1.0630\n  shrink=0.1, alpha= 1000: MAE=14.4875 +/- 1.0642\n  shrink=0.1, alpha=10000: MAE=14.5148 +/- 1.0697\n  shrink=0.2, alpha=  100: MAE=14.3180 +/- 1.0572\n  shrink=0.2, alpha= 1000: MAE=14.3415 +/- 1.0596\n  shrink=0.2, alpha=10000: MAE=14.3993 +/- 1.0709\n  shrink=0.3, alpha=  100: MAE=14.1778 +/- 1.0516\n  shrink=0.3, alpha= 1000: MAE=14.2130 +/- 1.0553\n  shrink=0.3, alpha=10000: MAE=14.3043 +/- 1.0727\n  shrink=0.5, alpha=  100: MAE=13.9533 +/- 1.0400\n  shrink=0.5, alpha= 1000: MAE=14.0110 +/- 1.0462\n  shrink=0.5, alpha=10000: MAE=14.1774 +/- 1.0754\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
